cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite the accompanying paper once it is available."
title: "SAS: Stable-Assignment Splitting for Sparse Triangular Accelerators"
abstract: >-
  Compiler transformation that preserves original-row compute-unit assignments
  and submitted relative order while allocating only newly introduced partial
  sums during long-row splitting for shared-memory sparse triangular solve
  accelerators. Includes RTL repair patches, physical-implementation and
  power-estimation flows, and independent checkers.
keywords:
  - sparse triangular solve
  - dataflow accelerator
  - graph transformation
  - task mapping
  - compiler scheduling
license: MIT
authors:
  - family-names: "SAS"
    given-names: "The"
preferred-citation:
  type: article
  title: "SAS: Stable-Assignment Splitting for Sparse Triangular Accelerators"
